+[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m## Behavior[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                               [49m
+[48;5;237m                                                                                                                                                                                                                            [49m
+[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m### Documents[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                             [49m
+[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m- `create(id, content)` stores a new document. Throws if the ID already exists on the current branch.[39m                                                                                                                     [49m
+[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m- `get(id)` returns the current content. Throws if the document doesn't exist or has been deleted.[39m                                                                                                                        [49m
+[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m- `update(id, content)` replaces the document content and creates a new version. Throws if the document doesn't exist.[39m                                                                                                    [49m
+[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m- `delete(id)` removes a document from the current branch. Throws if it doesn't exist.[39m                                                                                                                                    [49m
+[48;5;237m                                                                                                                                                                                                                            [49m
+[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m### Version History[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                       [49m
+[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m- Every `create` and `update` generates a new version with a unique `id`, a `timestamp`, and the full document `content` at that point.[39m                                                                                   [49m
+[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m- `getHistory(id)` returns versions in chronological order (oldest first).[39m                                                                                                                                                [49m
+[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m- `getVersion(id, versionId)` returns the content at a specific version.[39m                                                                                                                                                  [49m
+[48;5;237m                                                                                                                                                                                                                            [49m
+[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m### Branching[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                             [49m
+[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m- The default branch is `"main"`.[39m                                                                                                                                                                                         [49m
+[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m- `createBranch(name)` creates a new branch from the current branch's current state. If `fromBranch` is provided, branch from that branch instead.[39m                                                                        [49m
+[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m- `switchBranch(name)` switches the active branch. All subsequent CRUD operations apply to that branch.[39m                                                                                                                   [49m
+[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m- Changes on one branch are not visible on other branches.[39m                                                                                                                                                                [49m
+[48;5;237m                                                                                                                                                                                                                            [49m
+[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m### Merging[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                               [49m
+[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m- `merge(sourceBranch)` merges changes from `sourceBranch` into the current branch.[39m                                                                                                                                       [49m
+[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m- Uses **three-way merge**: find the common ancestor state (the point where the branches diverged), then compare both branches against that base.[39m                                                                         [49m
+[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m- For each document that changed on either branch:[39m                                                                                                                                                                        [49m
+[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m  - If only one side changed a field, take that change (no conflict).[39m                                                                                                                                                     [49m
+[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m  - If both sides changed the same field to the **same** value, no conflict.[39m                                                                                                                                              [49m
+[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m  - If both sides changed the same field to **different** values, that's a conflict.[39m                                                                                                                                      [49m
+[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m- If there are **no conflicts**, the merge is auto-applied to the current branch (`applied: true`), and the `merged` field contains the resulting document contents.[39m                                                      [49m
+[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m- If there **are conflicts**, the merge is **not** applied (`applied: false`), and the conflicts are returned so the caller can resolve them. The current branch remains unchanged.[39m                                       [49m
+[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m- The `merged` field always contains the merge result (with conflicts resolved in favor of "ours" for the purpose of showing what it would look like).[39m                                                                    [49m
+[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m- A merge with no changes on either side is a no-op (fast-forward).[39m                                                                                                                                                       [49m
+[48;5;237m                                                                                                                                                                                                                            [49m
+[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m## Constraints[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                            [49m
+[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m- All operations are synchronous and in-memory.[39m                                                                                                                                                                           [49m
+[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m- Documents are plain JSON objects (no arrays at the top level, though fields may contain arrays).[39m                                                                                                                        [49m
+[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m- Deep clone document contents on storage and retrieval to prevent mutation.[39m                                                                                                                                              [49m
+[48;5;237m  [38;5;231m- The store must handle multiple documents independently -- changes to different documents on different branches should merge cleanly with no conflicts.[39m                                                                  [49m
